  "notes": "{揺|ゆ}らす means to shake, rock, or sway something back and forth.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {揺|ゆ}れる (intransitive, to sway)\n- Pattern: Xを{揺|ゆ}らす (shake X)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{揺|ゆ}らしている means \"is shaking\" (ongoing action).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {体|からだ}を{揺|ゆ}らす: to sway one's body\n- ゆりかごを{揺|ゆ}らす: to rock a cradle\n- {心|こころ}を{揺|ゆ}らす: to move someone emotionally\n- {肩|かた}を{揺|ゆ}らして{笑|わら}う: to laugh while shaking one's shoulders\n\nCONTRAST:\n- {揺|ゆ}らす: to shake (transitive, gentle/rhythmic)\n- {揺|ゆ}する: to shake (transitive, more forceful, often to extort)\n- {振|ふ}る: to swing, wave (more vigorous movement)",
